&lt;p&gt;# Comments: 0&lt;/p&gt;</description><guid isPermaLink="false">https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49933819</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 14:18:34 +0000</pubDate></item><item><title>Ask HN: I think the AI terminology needs a reset</title><link>https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49933750</link><description>&lt;p&gt;A friend asked me what a personal AI agent does. I started explaining, then I realized I was describing three different things.&lt;p&gt;I think we need better order and terms in this world.&lt;p&gt;So personal ai agent can be 3 different things..&lt;p&gt;Delegate agent: It's own inbox, number, and accounts.
Like: "Hi, i'm Peter the agent of Ana, I'd like a table for four"&lt;p&gt;Twin agent: My accounts, but it says an agent is speaking.
Like: "Hi, I'm Ana, through her agent, I'd like a table for four"&lt;p&gt;Ghost agent: My accounts, without mentioning AI.
Like: "Hi, I'm Ana, I'd like a table for four"&lt;p&gt;Also the term "personal ai agent", I'm not sure if its the right term, 
like i think what makes this agent special that its "always on" right? 
not that its personal.. theoretically it can work for entire team..&lt;p&gt;I would like to know what you think and if you have better ideas&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr /&gt;
